Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 12:14:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 100/105] P1: singleton-route pruning for the MoE grouped GEMM

SGLANG_MOE_PRUNE_SINGLETON_TAU masks routes that are the only user of their
expert and below tau in routing weight, so the grouped GEMM reads fewer
distinct expert weights (~1.6 us of GEMM1+GEMM2 per expert dropped).  One
single-CTA Triton kernel over the [M, k] top-k tensors, in place, no host sync,
CUDA-graph safe.  Masked routes get expert id -1, which FlashInfer's prologue
sorts past num_valid_tokens and the finalize skips explicitly.  Default off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
